## 4. Magento's Built-In Widgets

Core widgets live under `lib/web/mage/` or `vendor/magento/module-ui/view/base/web/js/`. Here are the most important ones.

### 4.1 `mage.accordion`

**File:** `lib/web/mage/accordion.js`
**Extends:** `mage.tabs` (which extends `mage.collapsible`)

```javascript
// mage.accordion's own options (inherits more from mage.tabs and mage.collapsible)
{
    active: [0],              // ARRAY — indexes of active panels (not a single number)
    multipleCollapsible: false, // Allow multiple panels open simultaneously
    openOnFocus: false
    // Inherited from mage.collapsible: collapsible: true, openedState: null, animate: false
}
```

```html
<!-- HTML structure expected by mage.accordion -->
<div data-mage-init='{"mage/accordion": {"active": [0], "collapsible": true}}'>
    <div data-role="collapsible">
        <div data-role="trigger"><span>Section 1</span></div>
        <div data-role="content">Content of section 1</div>
    </div>
    <div data-role="collapsible">
        <div data-role="trigger"><span>Section 2</span></div>
        <div data-role="content">Content of section 2</div>
    </div>
</div>
```

### 4.2 `mage.tabs`

**File:** `lib/web/mage/tabs.js`

```html
<div data-mage-init='{"mage/tabs": {"active": [0]}}'>
    <ul>
        <li data-role="collapsible">
            <a data-toggle="trigger" href="#tab1">Tab 1</a>
        </li>
        <li data-role="collapsible">
            <a data-toggle="trigger" href="#tab2">Tab 2</a>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <div id="tab1" data-role="content">Tab 1 content</div>
    <div id="tab2" data-role="content">Tab 2 content</div>
</div>
```

### 4.3 `mage.dropdownDialog`

**File:** `lib/web/mage/dropdown.js`
**Widget name:** `mage.dropdownDialog` (NOT `mage.dropdown`)
**RequireJS alias:** `'dropdownDialog'` maps to `'mage/dropdown'`

> **Important:** The widget defined in `lib/web/mage/dropdown.js` is `$.widget('mage.dropdownDialog', $.ui.dialog, {...})` — it extends jQuery UI Dialog. There is **no** `mage.dropdown` widget. The short alias `'dropdown'` actually maps to `'mage/dropdowns'` (a different file).

```javascript
// Key options for mage.dropdownDialog
{
    triggerEvent: 'click',          // Event to open the dialog
    triggerTarget: null,            // Selector of the trigger element
    triggerClass: null,             // Class added to trigger when open
    parentClass: null,              // Class added to parent element when open
    defaultDialogClass: 'mage-dropdown-dialog',
    closeOnMouseLeave: true,        // Close when mouse leaves the dialog
    closeOnClickOutside: true,      // Close when clicking outside
    autoOpen: false,
    bodyClass: '',                  // Class added to body when open
    modal: false
}
```

### 4.4 `mage.modal`

**File:** `vendor/magento/module-ui/view/base/web/js/modal/modal.js`
**RequireJS module ID:** `Magento_Ui/js/modal/modal`
**Note:** There is NO `lib/web/mage/modal.js`.

```javascript
// Key options (verified against actual codebase)
{
    type: 'popup',          // 'popup', 'slide', 'custom'
    title: '',              // Modal title
    modalClass: '',         // Additional CSS class
    buttons: [...],         // Array of button config objects (has default close button)
    responsive: false,      // NOTE: default is false, not true
    innerScroll: false,
    trigger: '',            // Selector of trigger element
    autoOpen: false         // Open immediately on init
}
```

```html
<!-- Basic modal example — use Magento_Ui/js/modal/modal as the module ID -->
<div data-mage-init='{
    "Magento_Ui/js/modal/modal": {
        "type": "popup",
        "title": "My Modal",
        "buttons": [{
            "text": "Close",
            "class": "action-primary",
            "click": "closeModal"
        }]
    }
}'>
    <p>Modal content goes here.</p>
</div>
```

### 4.5 `mage.loader`

**File:** `lib/web/mage/loader.js`
**RequireJS alias:** `'loader'` → `'mage/loader'`

```javascript
// Show the loader
$('body').loader('show');

// Hide the loader
$('body').loader('hide');
```

```html
<!-- Initialize loader on body -->
<script type="text/x-magento-init">
{
    "body": {
        "mage/loader": {}
    }
}
</script>
```

**Exam focus:**
- `mage.modal` has three types: `popup`, `slide`, `custom`. Know them.
- `mage.modal` is in `Magento_Ui/js/modal/modal` — **not** in `lib/web/mage/`.
- `mage.loader` is initialized on `body` and controlled programmatically via `show`/`hide` methods.
- `data-role` attributes are used by `accordion` and `tabs` to identify trigger/content elements.

