## 10. How Magento Loads Widgets (The Bootstrap Chain)

Understanding this helps when debugging why a widget doesn't initialize.

```
Browser loads page HTML
        |
        v
RequireJS loads and executes
        |
        v
'mage/bootstrap' is auto-required via deps in Magento_Theme's requirejs-config.js
        |
        v
'mage/apply/main' scans the DOM for:
  [1] <script type="text/x-magento-init">  blocks
  [2] Elements with [data-mage-init] attributes
        |
        v
For each found component:
  - Parses the JSON configuration
  - Requires the module via RequireJS
  - When module loads: calls widget initializer on target element
        |
        v
Widget _create() and _init() run
        |
        v
UI is interactive
```

### RequireJS Module Path Mapping

Magento maps short module paths to full file paths in `requirejs-config.js`. The actual aliases defined in `Magento_Theme/view/frontend/requirejs-config.js` include:

```javascript
// vendor/magento/module-theme/view/frontend/requirejs-config.js
var config = {
    map: {
        '*': {
            'accordion':      'mage/accordion',
            'tabs':           'mage/tabs',
            'collapsible':    'mage/collapsible',
            'dropdownDialog': 'mage/dropdown',    // mage.dropdownDialog widget
            'dropdown':       'mage/dropdowns',   // different file — NOT mage/dropdown
            'loader':         'mage/loader',
            'tooltip':        'mage/tooltip',
            'menu':           'mage/menu',
            'validation':     'mage/validation/validation'
            // NOTE: there is NO short alias for 'modal' — use full path: Magento_Ui/js/modal/modal
        }
    },
    deps: [
        'mage/common',
        'mage/dataPost',
        'mage/bootstrap'    // auto-loaded here — no layout XML needed
    ]
};
```

**Exam focus:**
- Widget initialization is **asynchronous** — it happens after RequireJS loads all dependencies.
- Do not expect widgets to be available synchronously after DOM load without RequireJS wrapping.
- `mage/apply/main` is the bootstrapper that processes both `data-mage-init` and `x-magento-init`.
- There is **no** short alias `'modal'` — always use `'Magento_Ui/js/modal/modal'` as the full path.
- The alias `'dropdownDialog'` → `'mage/dropdown'`; the alias `'dropdown'` → `'mage/dropdowns'` (different file).

